      "writtenOn": "2023-02-10T14:52:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve copied this from the follow up change as while reviewing that change is what caused me to see this, it actually applies to this change:\n\n\u003e I think the fact that you are using the same properties structure for java_import and java_sdk_library_import as you use for java_library and java_sdk_library is a mistake. It causes complications in the testing and the code because you need profile_guided for prebuilts and profile for sources and certain combinations don\u0027t make sense and you have to test for them.\n\u003e \n\u003e It would be easier to have a separate import specific structure for dexpreopting.",
      "revId": "46a12c0551219e3ef3a84cbac7db3100f333d480",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6f205233_e8aa6def",
        "filename": "java/dexpreopt.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 133,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-10T14:39:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of ignoring it can you check if it is set and then fail instead?",
      "revId": "46a12c0551219e3ef3a84cbac7db3100f333d480",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0c0cd6ee_afa377de",
        "filename": "java/dexpreopt.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 242,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-10T14:39:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of refactoring this so it can be called from `PopulateFromVariant`, which over complicates this and makes it work differently to what most people would expect I recommend that you just store the result of calling this from dexpreopt in `blueprint:\"mutated\"` tagged fields in the `dexpreoptProperties` struct and access that from the `PopulateFromVariant` method.\n\nIt avoids duplicate work, simplifies this code and simplifies the `PopulateFromVariant` method.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 242,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 242,
        "endChar": 93
      },
      "revId": "46a12c0551219e3ef3a84cbac7db3100f333d480",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6596e87d_fa5263a4",
        "filename": "java/java.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 805,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-10T14:39:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using the same structure here as is used for the source module is not a good idea. I know it is annoying to have to duplicate parts of the structure but it is safer and easier to maintain longer term.\n\nIt is safer because only those fields you specifically want can be passed through to the snapshot. It would be very easy to add a new property into the struct and start passing it through to the snapshot without tagging it to prevent it being written out for previous releases. Having a separate struct makes that a separate change, and makes it clearer that these are special.\n\nIt is easier to maintain because at some point in future you will want to add more fields that need to be passed through to the snapshot, or customize the behavior. That will require that you tag the fields within this structure with `supported_build_releases:\"V+\"` or some other tag that is used by the sdk snapshot code and they will cause issues as the blueprint parsing code may not recognize them.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 805,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 805,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "46a12c0551219e3ef3a84cbac7db3100f333d480",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2d0e8076_dd5658d4",
        "filename": "java/java.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 857,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-10T14:39:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is very dangerous as it makes it extremely easy to pass additional properties that are not supported on earlier releases through to the sdk snapshot.\n\nThe only structures that should be passed through like this are atomic structures (like apex/module pairs).",
      "revId": "46a12c0551219e3ef3a84cbac7db3100f333d480",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
